186045417] [17592186259637 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259637 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13d7af34-5a26-56da-8335-dcbefb3a99a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259637 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic terms ${u}^{2}$ and ${v}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4u+6v \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299946 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299946 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299946 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "041da615-473a-59b3-bd74-078cc5cac382" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300150 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4t+4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300150 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300150 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "278a088d-66ff-5fc3-9def-6ae04de020b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300484 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300484 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300484 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "67ce37ea-b2ab-5a58-86f8-69d3f8240639" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300820 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300820 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300820 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ab0ec50a-1d0e-532d-ab8d-7cf840b59340" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301157 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4t+4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301157 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301157 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f2329096-2544-59c2-a74f-b394b5ad02bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186299946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186301157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186299946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301808 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b1a16360-6703-53e1-9901-03f44bb4aa65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306621 #edb/ref 1080 "3{e}^{-2x}+2\\operatorname{cos}(3x)+3\\operatorname{sin}(3x)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306621 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306621 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9d79074e-27e9-5f57-9e8f-e7df67ac74b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307799 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186306621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307799 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307799 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307799 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186306621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307799 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "59c70ecc-7755-5121-a34e-713ab4626109" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308363 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308363 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333044" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308363 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308363 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+2y=13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\,y(0)=5\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+2y=13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}=A{e}^{-2x},$ solve the initial value problem.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308363 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58d13845-465e-5368-a086-659bbbd2ba3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308363 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+2{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}=-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+2(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))=13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(3\\beta +2\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(-3\\alpha +2\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)=13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\beta +2\\alpha =13\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ -3\\alpha +2\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =2,\\beta =3.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=5$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-2\\cdot 0}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =5 \\\\ A+2+0 & =5 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=3{e}^{-2x}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339374 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339374 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339374 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1c87faa6-b893-53ba-92f4-903ccf2dd32d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339603 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339603 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339603 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "359295b0-82ba-5167-85b6-7dd0bfdb6bf5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339993 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339993 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339993 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "60eaf115-9b83-5456-8a7e-58465ef148d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340021 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340021 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340021 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "64ccd9c1-b048-5406-90fe-2f5854979f7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340075 #edb/ref 1080 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 16\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340075 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340075 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6ac239fb-67c1-5152-911c-d8d3251c0f0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341624 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341624 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341624 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218634